WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.779 --> 00:00:04.170
This is one of Delta's largest kitchen facilities in America.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.130
Around 3201st class meals and flight fuel boxes are prepared and packaged 

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.739
daily for domestic flights out of Atlanta's Hartsfield Jackson Airport.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.250
And thanks to a recent $54 million renovation and a partnership with catering 

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:18.850
company.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:24.159
Newest Delta is testing out these new robotic machines helping the team of 1100 

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.049
employees get everything ready by take off.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.130
The 120,000 square foot facility can be broken down into several stations.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:38.209
So everything you see in this fridge was delivered this morning and it will go through production and we will be on flights today.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.650
If not the latest tomorrow,

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.479
the kitchen gets its full order of meals 24 hours before a flight.

00:00:43.619 --> 00:00:48.509
We put receiving dates on the container and that's where it goes through into the first process of 

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.330
the production.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.439
Raw ingredients are soaked in a sanitizing solution for 90 seconds and anyone 

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.299
handling food suits up then goes through a handed shoe wash before 

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.930
heading to the core of the facility.

00:01:01.169 --> 00:01:03.659
The hot and cold kitchens here,

00:01:03.669 --> 00:01:07.050
chefs have to prep and cook nearly 40 different meal components.

00:01:07.279 --> 00:01:08.190
On average,

00:01:08.199 --> 00:01:12.760
the facility can go through about £400 of cherry tomatoes and £5100 of 

00:01:12.769 --> 00:01:14.050
broccolini in a month.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.970
I would say the most challenging aspect is the scale of our business.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.830
Part of the $54 million renovation included industrial appliances to shorten cook 

00:01:22.839 --> 00:01:27.625
times like this pressurized brat pan which can cook £40 of orzo in 

00:01:27.635 --> 00:01:28.934
15 minutes.

00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:33.764
And these rational ovens that can be programmed to monitor the temperature of the food inside to 

00:01:33.775 --> 00:01:36.955
ensure a proper cook timing is key.

00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:40.055
Everything needs to be packed for delivery by take off.

00:01:40.184 --> 00:01:42.095
So we're here in our production area.

00:01:42.105 --> 00:01:42.885
As you see here,

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:47.495
we have a screen which gives us basically a status update on all of our flight departures.

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:48.894
So you can see here,

00:01:48.904 --> 00:01:53.639
the dock will tell us exactly which dock that flight will depart from which truck number has been 

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:57.959
assigned to that departure K RT stands for kitchen ready time.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.209
So that will tell us exactly when we have to have all of our flights ready,

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.150
all of the equipment,

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.970
all of the food packed ready to be departed exactly at that time to ensure we have an on site 

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.149
on time departure.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.960
Each station in the production area is dedicated to packaging one specific dish 

00:02:13.059 --> 00:02:14.539
with a visual reference.

00:02:14.729 --> 00:02:18.149
The food is one hour maximum that can be out on the tables for production.

00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:22.292
We then make sure that we keep that maintained that temperature for tray assembly.

00:02:22.302 --> 00:02:25.473
The team gets a helping hand from this automated robot system.

00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:29.363
We just started the journey a few months ago and with robotics,

00:02:29.373 --> 00:02:34.223
we can get consistency on that tray which frees us up for our 

00:02:34.233 --> 00:02:39.093
people and the people in the kitchen to go and make sure that the quality is there 

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:41.072
and the safety is there as well.

00:02:41.082 --> 00:02:45.776
A Delta representative said the company looked to robots to take over repetitive 

00:02:45.785 --> 00:02:49.895
tasks like assembling on flight trays on one side,

00:02:49.906 --> 00:02:54.865
food is placed onto a conveyor belt and stamped with the date of when the meal was made on the 

00:02:54.876 --> 00:02:55.455
other.

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:58.936
The robot places cutlery napkins and side dishes.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:02:59.815
In one hour,

00:02:59.826 --> 00:03:02.656
the robot can assemble 750 trays.

00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:03.356
Finally,

00:03:03.365 --> 00:03:08.065
the trays are packed into the carts which have been sanitized in this steam powered machine at 

00:03:08.076 --> 00:03:09.445
170 F.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.449
And in a single hour,

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.250
this machine can clean around 250 cars.

00:03:14.779 --> 00:03:16.050
By the end of the day,

00:03:16.059 --> 00:03:20.419
the facility will break down then rebuild up to 8100 carts and 

00:03:20.429 --> 00:03:21.250
carriers.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.990
Once the meals are packed into the clean carts,

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.130
they're held in a refrigerator,

00:03:25.324 --> 00:03:29.794
holding space until they are loaded into insulated trucks for final transport.

00:03:29.815 --> 00:03:32.695
The trucks are coming in and out to and from aircraft all day.

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:36.994
Every day loads start at four AM and end at 9 30 PM.

00:03:37.074 --> 00:03:40.195
Their final destination some 350 flights a day,

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.779
hot meals are heated up in flight.

00:03:42.929 --> 00:03:47.080
A Delta representative said that this facility could be the facility of the future,

00:03:47.089 --> 00:03:49.839
combining technology with the human workforce.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.759
The company declined to state where they might roll out the robotic equipment in the future.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.229
We're in the food business,

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.220
60 million meals a year for us.

00:03:58.229 --> 00:04:01.845
It's the future is all about just to innovate in that space,

00:04:01.854 --> 00:04:06.074
whether it's new equipment in our kitchens down to really 

00:04:06.085 --> 00:04:08.225
personalization for the customer.

00:04:08.345 --> 00:04:13.074
Delta did not provide comment on how the food and beverage program affects ticket prices,

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.595
but its food offerings depend on a few things.

00:04:15.675 --> 00:04:20.005
How long your flight is your travel class and what city you're flying out of?

00:04:20.535 --> 00:04:22.204
And as long as planes are flying,

00:04:22.214 --> 00:04:23.904
this facility won't stop,

00:04:24.445 --> 00:04:26.924
they are making meals seven days a week,

00:04:26.984 --> 00:04:28.165
all year round.

